+# Unit43 — Backend-owned raw asset import (pending Actions)
+
+## Source/PlusCal and policy audit
+
+Continue fully read development-policy.md v0.2.6/AGENT.md; unchanged. Source45 assets.py importProjectFilesToDirectory/importProjectFileToSlot allows Application pure byte reads/parse and completed chooser values, but prohibits Application project candidates or Backend UI callbacks. Backend assets_files.py buildProjectAssetImportCandidate and common project_efsm.py send own current target/directory/collision/id/reference, validation/source retry/one commit; domain parse/collision/validation failure returns noncommit. Pseudocode BuildAssetImportInAttempt/ConnectDataInsideCandidate and public assets procedures directly specify final path/replaceId choices (no invented proposal protocol), raw data/image only, unique batch paths/current same-kind replacement identity, graph-only data connection/image-only image link, input-order facts and official copied success reads. Source45/pseudocode23 unchanged; no new meaning needed.
+
+## Coherent ownership cutover / prompt-to-artifact checklist
+
+- ASSETS_IMPORTED handler no longer reads payload.candidate/imported. Private buildProjectAssetImportCandidate resolves explicit current directory/visible target, copies canonical slot content, revalidates final plans/current ownership/reservations, mints current next IDs, stages copied bytes inside candidate, connects target and rebuilds affected editable graphs within candidate.
+- Directory and slot producers now complete copied path/replaceId choices, await and copy file bytes, then dispatch files/directory/choices/optional targetSlotId only. Empty directory input returns[] before chooser/read/command; cancel returns None. A pure copied byte-read before synchronous command is already permitted by Source; no unnecessary async EFSM or runtime bridge.
+- Entire candidate validates before source identity comparison. Changed authority discards draft/facts and recalculates all; one commit only. Known parse/model and invariant validation failures return noncommit, not partial mutations/rollback. No broad catch over public chooser/IO/postcommit queries. Actual input-order imported path/id/owners and changed IDs feed reconciliation and official success queries. Replaced image resources release only after commit; unrelated URLs are not released wholesale.
+- Image link preserves slot-local settings/caption/extension/chart payload per existing Source; it does not reset slot or silently change its type. Data requires graph target and appends same-candidate real CSV object. Noneditable graph rejects; no chart rebuild/activate mutation after commit in Application.
+- Case116: minimal prepared input shape, empty/cancel, one batch commit/two original-order immutable query returns, copied bytes do not alias authority, later parse rejection atomic/no useful work, noncommit gating.
+- Case117: image asset/link one commit/settings/extensions; validation noncommit; authority replacement during validation recalculates next CSV ID and chart connection; late success query throw keeps commit and skips later useful render work.
+
+## Pending evidence and limits
+
+Code94 stale, unchanged upper45/23 lineage; staged Git blob fingerprint sha256:2a28ac11cb5eae343d60ff4787c443b7038a7ee947ce1d5e80913ddcd1b03c01 not a local checker pass. New exact-SHA117+117/repeat/build/canonical+cumulative/fidelity PENDING; no local app/test/build/checker and no TLC claim. Existing aggregate dashboard renderer is not supplied-state aligned by this unit. Raw top-level router/legacy loader entrypoints and other CSV/image replace/connection/package import handlers still require whole-owner audit; do not infer their conformance from these two producer cutovers. Schema/serializer/raster/dashboard/lifecycle/timing and complete goal audit remain open. Tests for current collision introduced after completed choices/byte-await target changes and copied original image replacement resource boundaries should be checked during coverage review before bounded closure; prior115 query tests are not import-command proof.
